  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration Information Center - MICenter</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lithuania has seen a substantial rise in its foreign population since joining the EU in 2004, with foreigners now constituting 7.1% of theountry&apos;s population, totaling 203,000 individuals. Half of these foreigners entered for labor purposes, while 25% are Ukrainians under EU temporary protection.   This surge has prompted a need for effective integration measures. Foreigners in Lithuania commonly face challenges such as complex administrative procedures, lack of information in Russian and limited support services. Institutions often lack multilingual resources, creating a need for centralized, multilingual information. In response, the Migration Information Center aims to alleviate these challenges by providing essential information, personalized consultations, mental health support, and enhancing the capacity of stakeholders involved in migrants&apos; integration. The project&apos;s overarching objective is to facilitate the integration and enhance the inclusion of foreigners in Lithuania through a one-stop-shop approach for third-country nationals (TCNs) and stateless persons.</narrative>
  </description>
